Fruits to Enjoy During Your Period

Fruits are an easy and refreshing addition to your meals during your period. They require very little preparation and can provide carbohydrates, fibre, vitamins, minerals, and water. Instead of looking for one special fruit that promises to solve every period symptom, it is better to enjoy a variety of fruits as part of your normal diet.

Bananas are one of the most convenient choices. You can eat one on its own, slice it over oatmeal, mix it into yoghurt, or blend it into a smoothie. It is also easy to carry when you are heading to college, work, or travelling.

Oranges are another useful choice. Citrus fruits provide vitamin C, which supports the absorption of iron from plant-based foods. If your meal contains lentils, beans, chickpeas, or spinach, adding a vitamin C-rich fruit can be a simple way to complement the meal.

Guava is also naturally rich in vitamin C and makes a convenient snack. You can simply cut it into pieces and enjoy it during the afternoon.

Watermelon is a refreshing option because of its high water content. It can be especially enjoyable during warm weather. Eating water-rich fruits can contribute to your overall fluid intake, although drinking water remains important.

Papaya, apples, pears, grapes, pomegranate, and berries can also be included. You do not need expensive imported fruits. Seasonal and locally available fruits can be excellent choices and are often easier to include regularly.

If you want your fruit snack to be more filling, combine it with protein or healthy fats. Try an apple with peanut butter, banana with yoghurt, or berries with oats and yoghurt. These combinations can help create a more balanced snack.

Fruit can also be used to satisfy sweet cravings. Instead of trying to completely eliminate sweet foods during your period, you can include naturally sweet fruits alongside your favourite treats. There is no need to feel guilty about enjoying dessert occasionally.

Hydration is another part of period care. Along with fruit and water, soups and other suitable beverages can contribute to your fluid intake. Pay attention to your thirst and drink regularly throughout the day.

Good menstrual hygiene can make your period routine more comfortable too. Choose a sanitary pad appropriate for your flow and change it regularly. Carrying a spare pad in your handbag or backpack is also useful when you are away from home.

